<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="002" project="dotnet-10-upgrade-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>Retarget Spaarke.Scheduling to net10 FIRST (warnings-as-errors) + clear NU1510/SYSLIB</title>
    <phase>P0 Retarget + build-green</phase>
    <gate>001 complete</gate>
    <status>completed</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Modifies .csproj build config; TreatWarningsAsErrors makes every NU1510/SYSLIB a build error; brownfield root-cause.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Mechanical retarget fully specified by design §3.1/§5; the judgment (which pins are superseded) is bounded and enumerated.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>xhigh</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Serial P0 chain; must land before the other libs so warnings-as-errors surface NU1510/SYSLIB early on the smallest project.</parallel-reason>
    <deps>001</deps>
    <tags>dotnet, migration, packages, bff-api</tags>
    <estimated-effort>2-3 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Retarget `Spaarke.Scheduling` from net8.0 to net10.0 FIRST, because it sets `TreatWarningsAsErrors=true` — so any NU1510 (direct reference superseded by the net10 inbox) or SYSLIB obsolete warning is a hard build error there. Resolve every such warning by removing superseded CVE-pin `PackageReference`s (after confirming the inbox version ≥ the pinned CVE-fixed version) so this project compiles clean on net10. This is the canary that de-risks the rest of the retarget.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Expert in .NET SDK package resolution, NU1510, SYSLIB obsoletions, and MSBuild warning policy. Follow ADRs strictly.</role>
  <goal>`Spaarke.Scheduling.csproj` targets `net10.0`; `dotnet build -c Release src/server/shared/Spaarke.Scheduling/` is green with zero warnings (warnings-as-errors); every removed pin is documented with its inbox-version-≥-CVE-version justification in `notes/pin-removals.md`.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>design §3.1 flags `Spaarke.Scheduling` with `TreatWarningsAsErrors=true` → "handle first." design §5 H4 lists the superseded CVE pins (`System.Text.Json 8.0.5`, `System.Formats.Asn1 8.0.1`, `System.Security.Cryptography.Pkcs 8.0.1`, `System.Text.RegularExpressions 4.3.1`, `System.Security.Cryptography.Xml 8.0.4`) — remove only after confirming the net10 inbox version is ≥ the pinned CVE-fixed version. Root `Directory.Build.props` also carries `TreatWarningsAsErrors=true` with a `WarningsNotAsErrors` downgrade list — do not weaken it to force green.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/server/shared/Spaarke.Scheduling/Spaarke.Scheduling.csproj</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">Directory.Build.props</file>
      <file role="new">projects/dotnet-10-upgrade-r1/notes/pin-removals.md</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="001" status="pending">10.0.x SDK resolvable via global.json.</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: ONLY `Spaarke.Scheduling.csproj` (+ the pin-removals note). Do NOT retarget Core/Dataverse/BFF/tests in this task.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">MUST verify the net10 inbox version ≥ each pinned CVE-fixed version BEFORE removing that pin (spec FR-04). Record the evidence per pin. Keep any pin the framework does NOT supply.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">MUST NOT weaken `TreatWarningsAsErrors` or expand `WarningsNotAsErrors` to force a green build — resolve the root cause.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-029">No SelfContained / RID / trimming changes; framework-dependent only.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>.NET 10 inbox package supersession (NU1510) + SYSLIB obsoletions</topic>
    <files>
      <file>projects/dotnet-10-upgrade-r1/spec.md</file>
      <file>projects/dotnet-10-upgrade-r1/design.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-029-bff-publish-hygiene.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/azure-deployment.md</file>
    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="nu1510-pin-cleanup" location="projects/dotnet-10-upgrade-r1/design.md">design §5 H4 + §6.2 enumerate the superseded pins and the inbox-≥-pin verification rule.</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Load spec FR-01/FR-04 + design §5 H4. Declare RIGOR: FULL.</step>
    <step order="1">Change `Spaarke.Scheduling.csproj` `<TargetFramework>` to `net10.0`.</step>
    <step order="2">Run `dotnet build -c Release src/server/shared/Spaarke.Scheduling/`; capture every NU1510/SYSLIB warning-turned-error.</step>
    <step order="3">For each NU1510 (superseded direct reference), confirm the net10 inbox version ≥ the pinned CVE-fixed version (nuget.org / restore graph); if yes, remove the `PackageReference`; record the evidence in `notes/pin-removals.md`.</step>
    <step order="4">For each SYSLIB obsolete warning, note it — if it is a source-code obsoletion (e.g. X509 ctor) it belongs to task 012, not here; if it can be resolved by a package bump within scope, do so.</step>
    <step order="5">Re-build until green (zero warnings). Do NOT suppress; resolve.</step>
    <step order="6">Update `tasks/TASK-INDEX.md`: set 002 status to ✅.</step>
    <step order="7">Document any deviation in `projects/dotnet-10-upgrade-r1/notes/`.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If any NU1510 pin CANNOT be confirmed as inbox-≥-CVE (i.e. removing it would regress a CVE fix), STOP — do not remove it and do not suppress the error; surface it per CLAUDE.md §6 for a keep-the-pin decision.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <tools>
    <tool name="dotnet">Build + restore Spaarke.Scheduling</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="config">src/server/shared/Spaarke.Scheduling/Spaarke.Scheduling.csproj</output>
    <output type="doc">projects/dotnet-10-upgrade-r1/notes/pin-removals.md</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the retargeted csproj, when `dotnet build -c Release src/server/shared/Spaarke.Scheduling/` runs, then it succeeds with zero warnings (warnings-as-errors satisfied).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Every removed pin has a recorded inbox-version-≥-CVE-fixed-version justification in `notes/pin-removals.md`.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: `TreatWarningsAsErrors` and the root `WarningsNotAsErrors` list are unchanged (not weakened to force green).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: no other project's csproj is modified by this task.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>spec FR-01 (Scheduling first) + FR-04 (pin removal after inbox check). This is the canary — the pin-removal evidence collected here is reused by task 003 for Core/Dataverse.

  COMPLETION (2026-08-11): `Spaarke.Scheduling.csproj` TFM net8.0 → net10.0 (1-line change). `dotnet build -c Release src/server/shared/Spaarke.Scheduling/` → **0 warnings / 0 errors** (warnings-as-errors satisfied; also built Core+Dataverse deps at net8, valid consume-down). FINDING: Scheduling carries NO superseded CVE pins — the design §5 H4 pins (System.Text.Json 8.0.5 etc.) are actually in Core/Dataverse/BFF (tasks 003/004), NOT here. Scheduling's Microsoft.Extensions.* 8.0.x are ordinary class-library NuGet refs (not shared-framework-provided → no NU1510); Cronos is third-party. NO pins removed → escalation trigger did NOT fire. Solution-wide Extensions.*→10.0.x alignment DEFERRED to 003/004 (atomic graph move; bumping only Scheduling now would increase skew). Ledger: `notes/pin-removals.md`. Quality gates (9.5) SKIPPED — config-only (TFM bump) + doc note, not test-modifying. ADR-029 verified by inspection (no SelfContained/RID/Trim/AOT). Negative criteria: Directory.Build.props unchanged; only Scheduling.csproj modified (git diff = 1 file, 1 line).</notes>

  <execution>
    <skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill>
  </execution>
</task>
